A note on the latticed deity column:
The large column with many small deity figures embedded across its surface is iconographically significant but without clearer photography cannot be definitively identified. It may be a 万神柱 (wànshén zhù, "Ten-Thousand-Deity Column"), a form of cosmological deity display in which the entire column surface becomes an iconographic programme. This is different from a stupa or pagoda that houses deities within it — here the deities ARE the surface of the column. Flagged for fieldwork confirmation.
