The Five Military Generals (五兵軍 / 五營元帥) are the
celestial military commanders corresponding to the five
directions and five elements of Taoist cosmology:
  - East Marshall (東方軍)
  - South Marshall (南方軍)
  - West Marshall (西方軍)
  - North Marshall (北方軍)
  - Centre Marshall (中央軍)

Their collective function is cosmological protection
of the temple space and its compound from all directions
simultaneously — an apotropaic shield at compound scope.

Background: Qilin (麒麟) relief in silver/gold against red
  -- the qilin is a Chinese auspicious mythological creature
     associated with good governance and the protection
     of the righteous; its placement above the marshals
     surmounts their collective protective function with
     cosmological auspiciousness

