The bilateral pair is：
LEFT ALTAR (五兵軍 — Five Military Generals)
  Tradition:  Taoist
  Function:   cosmological spatial protection
              (five directions, apotropaic)
  Register:   martial, directional, protective

RIGHT ALTAR (六度教 — Bodhisattva above Tai Sui)
  Tradition:  Buddhist surmounting Taoist-folk
  Function:   cosmological temporal administration
              (sixty-year cycle) under Buddhist
              soteriological authority
  Register:   calendrical, fatalistic, interceded
The bilateral pair is now significantly richer than the previous reading. Both altars are cosmological in function, but they cover different axes of cosmological operation:
LEFT: spatial protection — five military generals
      guarding the five directions (space)

RIGHT: temporal administration — sixty Tai Sui
       governing the sixty-year cycle (time)
The bilateral pair encodes a cosmic protection programme that covers both spatial and temporal dimensions simultaneously. The temple's compound is protected in every direction by the Five Military Generals, and protected across every year of time by the Tai Sui. The Bodhisattva above the Tai Sui adds a third claim: that Buddhist compassion surmounts and intercedes within the temporal cosmic order.
